Title: 0011-aros-keymap-text-fallback
Repository: grafx2
Base-Commit: f84cb09dc59d706d6e7b28778b01ba911f52298c
Requires: 0010-sdl2-keysym-to-ansi-no-character.patch
Author: aros-grafx2 project
Date: 2026-09-25
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS SDL2 text fallback only; keyboard shortcuts still use GrafX2 keycodes.

Problem:
  AROS SDL2 does not emit SDL_TEXTINPUT, so GrafX2 used an unmodified SDLK symbol in text fields. Shifted punctuation, Caps Lock, and keymap-specific Alt/Amiga combinations therefore could not produce their configured characters.
Solution:
  Convert supported SDL keysyms and modifiers to an AROS raw-key InputEvent and call keymap.library MapRawKey. The active AROS keymap, rather than a hard-coded US shift table, supplies the text character; ordinary SDL2 platforms keep their existing mapping.
Validation:
  2026-09-25: ABIv11 cross-build against the AROS One SDK passed, including
  the keymap.library inline call. scripts/check-reproduction.sh passed with
  the complete series of 11 patches. Guest key-input verification not run.
Removal:
  Keep while AROS SDL2 does not provide SDL_TEXTINPUT. Remove when that
  backend provides the active keymap's text itself.

